abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC sonification of a classical phase-oscillator model. A sensor
  inside a simulated ring reads the local phase and the reading is
  rendered as audio (cos of the phase times local coherence); heart-like
  and brain-like scenes are pulse-arrival toys sonified as decaying
  thumps. Includes pre-registered, seeded studies with confidence
  intervals, including null and negative results. Not a recording, not
  an ECG or EEG, not a medical model, not a medical device. No listening
  test was run.
keywords:
  - sonification
  - toy-model
